fficiency gains outweigh the systemic risk of destabilizing labor markets that support a significant portion of the workforce. Until he accounts for the long-term degradation of human expertise and the loss of stable employment, his 'tax' argument remains a speculative justification for systemic disruption rather than a credible economic policy.",
